.TH REORDER-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-16" "reorder-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reorder-revamped \- drag a window tab along the tmux status line to move it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reorder-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.br
.B reorder-revamped
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B list
.br
.B reorder-revamped grab
.I session client
.br
.B reorder-revamped slide
.I session source target client measure
.br
.B reorder-revamped drop
.I session source:seen target activity
.br
.B reorder-revamped edge
.BR first | last | trailing
.I session source:seen activity
.br
.B reorder-revamped doctor
.br
.B reorder-revamped version
.br
.B reorder-revamped help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reorder-revamped
moves a tmux window when you drag its tab along the status line with the
mouse. In insert mode the tabs in between shift over, and the grabbed tab
slides under the pointer while you drag. The entry point
.B reorder-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, and every binding goes to tmux in one call.
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the status line mouse keys now.
.TP
.B list
Print every binding apply would make, one per line.
.TP
.BI grab " session client"
Measure every tab on the status line and write the format that maps the
pointer column to a window into
.BR @reorder_revamped_hit .
The drag binding runs it when a drag starts on tmux 3.8 and later.
.TP
.BI slide " session source target client measure"
Move the window
.I source
onto the tab of
.IR target ,
the tabs in between shifting over. With
.I measure
set to 1 it also writes the new hit format in the same tmux command.
.TP
.BI drop " session source:seen target activity"
Move the dragged window onto the tab it was released on, when the drag was
seen within the timeout.
.TP
.BI edge " first|last|trailing session source:seen activity"
Move the dragged window to the start or the end of the list, for a release on
status-left, status-right or the empty space.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, gum and the core tools. Exits 1 only when
a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-mode
or
.BR \-\-edges .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REORDER_REVAMPED_SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR REORDER_REVAMPED_MODE .
The command line wins over the environment, and the environment over the
tmux option.
.TP
.B REORDER_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B REORDER_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B REORDER_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B REORDER_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. Mode, live and edges are read when
the plugin loads.
.TP
.B @reorder_revamped_mode
.B insert
moves the window and shifts the ones in between;
.B swap
exchanges only the two windows, on release, with no live slide. The default is
.BR insert .
.TP
.B @reorder_revamped_live
.B off
keeps the tabs still while you drag and moves the window only on release. The
default is
.BR on .
.TP
.B @reorder_revamped_edges
.B off
leaves status-left, status-right and the empty space unbound. The default is
.BR on .
.TP
.B @reorder_revamped_timeout
Seconds of client activity after which a recorded drag is ignored, so a drag
abandoned over a pane cannot move a window on a later release. The default is
.BR 10 .
.TP
.B @reorder_revamped_enable_logging
.B 1
writes failed moves to
.IR ~/.tmux/reorder-revamped-logs/ .
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR gum (1)
